From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:16:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] ASoC: tas2764: keep the bus quiet while the amp is in
 hardware shutdown

The hwmon device is registered in the I2C probe, but the amp's SDZ line
is only raised in the component probe, when the sound card binds. In
between the amp is in hardware shutdown and does not acknowledge its
address, and a read of temp1_input or temp1_fault goes to the bus all
the same. On the 16-inch M5 Pro MacBook Pro (K116s), lm-sensors.service
runs "sensors" at boot; when it lands in that window, each of the six
amps fails two reads with EIO and the two speaker buses log

  i2c-apple 50501c000.i2c: Bus stuck, status 0x10210106
  i2c-apple 50501c000.i2c: Issuing reset due to status 0x08210106 (xfstatus 0x00000000)

six times each (status: NACK on the address byte). Whether it happens
depends on when the codec module's probe and the service meet, which is
why only some boots show it. The same holds after the component is
removed, when the amp's SDZ vote is dropped again.

Make the regmap cache-only from the I2C probe until the component probe
has raised SDZ, and again when the component probe fails or the
component is removed. A read of the volatile temperature register then
returns -EBUSY without a transfer; report that as "no data", like the
reading of an amp in software shutdown, so temp1_fault reads 1 instead
of failing. System sleep, where the regmap is cache-only as well, gets
the same answer.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Signed-off-by: Thomas Glanzmann <thomas@glanzmann.de>
---
omarchy-m5p-oled note (not part of the upstream commit):
Source: aurora-silicon/linux commit ad10208a01c67742900c2516a646d635bc56a333, pull request 1787
(open on 2026-11-14), unchanged. Tested upstream on a K116s ("11 of 11 boots clean").
Why here: half of the "no Bus stuck" pair. It only matters once a tree describes the speaker
amps; the K114s sound tree describes none, so this driver does not bind there. Carried so the
pair stays together.

 sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
index 887de3698..5a96c84e4 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
@@ -981,6 +981,13 @@ static int tas2764_read_die_temp(struct tas2764_priv *tas2764, long *result)
 	int ret, reg;
 
 	ret = regmap_read(tas2764->regmap, TAS2764_TEMP, &reg);
+	/*
+	 * The regmap is cache-only while the amp cannot be reached (SDZ low
+	 * before the component probe and after its removal, system sleep):
+	 * there is no reading then, as in software shutdown below.
+	 */
+	if (ret == -EBUSY)
+		return -ENODATA;
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 	/*
@@ -1108,6 +1115,9 @@ static int tas2764_codec_probe(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 
 	usleep_range(1000, 2000);
 
+	/* SDZ is high: the amp answers on the bus from here on */
+	regcache_cache_only(tas2764->regmap, false);
+
 	tas2764_reset(tas2764);
 	regmap_reinit_cache(tas2764->regmap, &tas2764_i2c_regmap);
 
@@ -1230,6 +1240,7 @@ static int tas2764_codec_probe(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 
 err_sdz:
 	/* Undo the power-up: ASoC doesn't call the remove after a failed probe */
+	regcache_cache_only(tas2764->regmap, true);
 	if (tas2764->sdz_gpio)
 		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(tas2764->sdz_gpio, 0);
 	/* As in the remove: no supply to drop with a GPIO SDZ, none left in a failed group */
@@ -1249,6 +1260,9 @@ static void tas2764_codec_remove(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 
 	tas2764_flush_shutdown(tas2764);
 
+	/* As before the probe: nothing reaches the amp once its SDZ vote is gone */
+	regcache_cache_only(tas2764->regmap, true);
+
 	/* A failed group's supply was forced off: there is no enable left to balance. */
 	if (tas2764_group_failed(tas2764))
 		return;
@@ -1658,6 +1672,14 @@ static int tas2764_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 		return result;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The amp is held in hardware shutdown (SDZ low) until the component
+	 * probe and does not acknowledge its address: keep everything that can
+	 * run before that, such as a read of the hwmon device registered below,
+	 * off the bus.
+	 */
+	regcache_cache_only(tas2764->regmap, true);
+
 	if (client->dev.of_node) {
 		result = tas2764_parse_dt(&client->dev, tas2764);
 		if (result)
